  "scopeNote": "General U.S. Army and Marine fictional male personnel candidates for 1935-1953. Given names are the SSA top 100 male names for U.S. births in 1900-1909, used as one relevant birth cohort, not a complete age distribution. Surnames are an editorial mixture of British, Irish, German, Jewish, Polish, Italian, French, Scandinavian, and Spanish-language forms found in American naming traditions; individual wartime usage remains unverified. Names do not assign ethnicity, race, religion, or immigration status. This general pool does not model the composition of any particular formation. Historically specific formations, including Japanese American units, require authored identities or a future dedicated profile. Date-sensitive segregation and integration are scenario-authoring context, not inferred from surnames.",
